  "id": "occupational-therapy",
  "term": "occupational therapy",
  "definition": "Occupational therapy is a rehabilitation approach that uses purposeful, personalized activities to improve limb function, support daily living skills, and help a person regain as much independence as possible. In the stroke context described here, it is used to support return to family, social, and work roles and may also improve perceptual and cognitive abilities.",
